{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion lag: The model consistently fails to anticipate sharp upward spikes (e.g., 70 to 76) and subsequent drops, treating volatile price action as a slow drift. Apply a momentum adjustment when the 3-day price change exceeds 2%.",
    "Adjust for sentiment disconnect: Positive sentiment spikes (value 1.00) in the history often precede immediate price drops or stagnation rather than the model's predicted gradual rise. Reduce forecast slope by 15-20% following a sentiment score of 1.00.",
    "Cap long-term horizon bias: The model exhibits a persistent upward bias in the 15-30 day horizon, predicting values 2-4 EUR higher than reality during consolidation phases. Apply a linear decay correction of -0.05 EUR per day beyond the 10-day mark.",
    "Overshoot correction after volatility: When history shows a rapid recovery from lows (e.g., 65 to 72), the model overestimates the sustainability of the rally. Reduce the forecast by 1.5 EUR if the 5-day volatility index is high and sentiment is neutral.",
    "Invert sentiment signal for short-term: A sentiment score of 1.00 in the immediate history (last 3 days) correlates with a price drop in the next 3 days. Apply a negative sentiment multiplier (-0.3) to the forecast for the first 3 days following such a signal."
  ]
}
